<h2 id="prices">What landing pages, websites and CRM systems cost</h2>
<p class="ed-intro">RESET development examples: NIVELLUX website, $600; SHEPIT HOUSE website, $1000; Estate CRM for DELMAR, $2000. These figures refer to specific agreed scopes. A new project is priced according to structure, content, features and integrations.</p>
<p>AI can accelerate parts of the work: prototyping, coding, testing individual solutions and repetitive operations. Savings depend on the product and what must be ready at handover.</p>
<p>One business needs a service page and contact details. Another needs a website for advertising, daily property uploads and enquiry delivery to sales.</p>
<div class="ed-price-grid" aria-label="Development cost examples"><div class="ed-price"><h3>NIVELLUX</h3><strong>$600</strong><p>Company website: services, projects and estimate enquiries.</p></div><div class="ed-price"><h3>SHEPIT HOUSE</h3><strong>$1000</strong><p>Development website with a site plan and instalment calculator.</p></div></div><p class="ed-note">Specific project costs reported by RESET, in US dollars. These are not universal tariffs.</p><table class="ed-table"><caption>Projects and development costs</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Project</th><th scope="col">Cost</th><th scope="col">Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="/en/cases/nivellux.html">NIVELLUX</a></td><td>$600</td><td>Services, portfolio, estimate requests, Russian and Spanish versions</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/en/cases/shepit-house.html">SHEPIT HOUSE</a></td><td>$1000</td><td>Website with site-plan selection and an instalment calculator</td></tr><tr><td><a href="/en/cases/delmar-custom-crm.html">Estate CRM for DELMAR</a></td><td>$2000</td><td>Enquiries, properties, selections and integrations</td></tr></tbody></table><p>The SHEPIT HOUSE figure covers website development. Advertising and other work in the wider case study are not included. New project scope and cost are agreed separately.</p>
<p>Even two landing pages can require very different effort. One client brings finished copy, photographs and a clear offer. Another needs product research, positioning, structure, materials and enquiry routing.</p>
<p>Page count is only a rough indicator. A single page with property matching, payment calculations and several integrations may require more work than a small informational website.</p>
<h2 id="formats">Using AI to build, building yourself and adding AI to a website</h2>
<p>Pricing discussions often mix three tasks.</p>
<p><strong>Building your own site with AI or a builder.</strong> The owner pays for tools and invests their time, making decisions about structure, content, services and checks.</p>
<p><strong>Hiring a team that uses AI.</strong> The client receives an agreed result; the team chooses the tools. This is the main focus here.</p>
<p><strong>Embedding AI in the product.</strong> Natural-language property search, a client assistant or automatic enquiry handling creates additional design, integration and testing work. Depending on the solution, model usage and data processing may carry recurring costs.</p>
<p>A site built with AI may have no AI features for visitors. Clarify that distinction when discussing the budget.</p>
<h2 id="ai-vs-classic">Is development with AI cheaper?</h2>
<p>With equivalent requirements, AI can reduce effort in particular stages. Savings depend on the task, team experience, source data and verification time.</p>
<p>A controlled GitHub Copilot experiment published in 2023 found that developers with AI access completed a JavaScript HTTP server task 55.8% faster than the control group. It demonstrates acceleration for that task, not a universal reduction in website budgets. <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.06590" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Copilot productivity study</a>.</p>
<p>Consider a hypothetical 100-hour project. If 40 hours of work can be completed twice as quickly and everything else stays the same, the project takes 80 hours: a 20% time saving.</p>
<figure class="ed-equation"><figcaption class="ed-eyebrow">Illustrative calculation / equivalent scope</figcaption><div class="ed-bar-row"><span>Original plan</span><div class="ed-bar">100 hours</div></div><div class="ed-bar-row"><span>Some tasks accelerated</span><div class="ed-bar ed-bar--after">80 hours</div></div><p class="ed-note">40 hours became 20; the remaining 60 stayed unchanged. Project saving: 20%. An arithmetic example, not a market forecast.</p></figure><p>Real estimates also include review, fixes and tool costs. The share of work that can be accelerated varies.</p>
<p>When comparing development with and without AI, compare equivalent features, design, integrations, testing and support. Mentioning AI in a proposal does not explain its price.</p>
<h2 id="business-goal">Where RESET starts</h2>
<p>We begin with the business objective: what the company wants after launch and how the product will be used daily.</p>
<p>For a website, we discuss the offer, audience and traffic. Will Google Ads run? Is organic search planned? Are separate pages needed for services, neighbourhoods or property types? Who handles enquiries?</p>
<p>These answers shape the structure before the first screen.</p>
<p>An agency advertising apartments in several areas may need dedicated landing pages and the selected property included in enquiries from the first version. A general destination would leave visitors searching for the advertised offer.</p>
<a class="ed-readmore" href="/en/materials/marketing/google-ads-nedvizhimost-2026/"><span><small>Related / RESET Journal</small>Connecting search queries, advertising and websites</span><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 19 19 5M5 5h14v14"/></svg></a><p>A CRM starts with staff workflows: who receives enquiries, how ownership is assigned, which statuses are used and what management needs to see.</p>
<p>Features and estimates follow that understanding.</p>
<h2 id="process">From business requirements to a working product</h2>
<p>RESET follows a sequence: objective, documentation, specification, prototype, implementation and verification.</p>
<p>Preparation scales with the project. A small landing page needs a compact brief; a custom CRM with roles and integrations needs more detail.</p>
<ol class="ed-process"><li><span class="ed-step">01</span><h3>Document the project</h3><p>Describe users, actions, data, external services and constraints.</p><p>For property websites, identify listing sources, update responsibility, languages and enquiry destinations. For a CRM, define entities, access and movement between stages.</p><p>Separate essential first-version features from later additions.</p><p class="ed-step-result">Outcome: a shared framework that the client and team can check for alignment.</p></li><li><span class="ed-step">02</span><h3>Prepare the specification</h3><p>Translate expectations into concrete requirements.</p><p>“Convenient search” needs detail: available parameters, filter combinations, no-results behaviour and shareable selection links.</p><p>For forms, define required fields, recipients, source tracking and error handling.</p><p class="ed-step-result">Outcome: a basis for estimating and acceptance, with clear implementation and verification criteria.</p></li><li><span class="ed-step">03</span><h3>Build a prototype</h3><p>Show the structure and journeys before full implementation.</p><p>Clients can find an offer, open a property, read terms and enquire; staff can test future CRM workflows.</p><p>Missing information, extra steps and awkward sequences are easier to spot. AI helps produce and change prototypes before all data and services are connected.</p><p class="ed-step-result">Outcome: agreed interface logic and key actions.</p></li><li><span class="ed-step">04</span><h3>Develop and connect systems</h3><p>Implement the interface and features, then connect data and services.</p><p>A website may need CMS, catalogue, forms, CRM and analytics. Internal systems may need roles, imports, history and automatic actions.</p><p>Agreed decisions make AI tasks more precise: the team knows required behaviour and constraints.</p><p class="ed-step-result">Outcome: a working version with agreed functionality and integrations.</p></li><li><span class="ed-step">05</span><h3>Verify journeys and prepare launch</h3><p>Test the actions the product exists to support.</p><p>For property enquiries, verify contact and property storage. For database updates, check prices and statuses. For analytics, compare events with actual actions.</p><p>Also check mobile behaviour, key-page speed and content management.</p><p>Agree account handover, maintenance and future changes for the project.</p><p class="ed-step-result">Outcome: a verified product and a clear post-launch process.</p></li></ol><figure class="ed-photo"><img src="/assets/reset-team-architecture.webp" width="1122" height="1402" loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Two specialists discuss a project plan at a table with a laptop"><figcaption>Agree structure and journeys before implementation. Editorial illustration.</figcaption></figure>
<h2 id="marketing">Why advertising and SEO should be considered early</h2>
<p>Traffic sources shape content and structure.</p>
<p>Search advertising needs to continue the user's intention after the click. Meta visitors may need more explanation after discovering an offer in their feed. Organic search needs pages planned around specific queries.</p>
<p>Requirements discovered after completion can force rework.</p>
<p>Separate campaign pages may be missing, the CMS may lack required fields, or forms may fail to pass the enquiry source.</p>
<p>We therefore clarify audience acquisition and measurement at the outset.</p>
<a class="ed-readmore" href="/en/materials/marketing/seo-nedvizhimost-2026/"><span><small>Related / RESET Journal</small>Building pages around search demand</span><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 19 19 5M5 5h14v14"/></svg></a><p>See <a href="/en/materials/marketing/meta-ads-nedvizhimost-2026/">Meta Ads for real estate</a> for lead quality and sales follow-up.</p>
<p>Technical SEO preparation and ongoing promotion have different scopes. Development does not automatically include regular articles, landing-page expansion and all organic acquisition work.</p>
<h2 id="content-design">How content, design and data affect price</h2>
<p>Content can represent a substantial share of the project.</p>
<p>Approved copy, photographs, specifications and translations can be used directly. Missing materials require positioning, writing, image selection and fact-checking.</p>
<p>AI helps draft alternatives. Actual purchase terms, service details, benefits and limitations must come from the business or verified sources.</p>
<p>A ready-made visual foundation and a custom interface also involve different workloads. Unique screens, component states, mobile adaptation and interactions affect estimates.</p>
<p>Property data deserves particular attention. Even existing exports can contain duplicates, inconsistent area names, missing fields or unavailable photographs. Preparation and checks belong in the plan.</p>
<p>Ask what each page contains and where it comes from, alongside how many pages there will be.</p>
<h2 id="self-build">When building with AI yourself makes sense</h2>
<p>Self-building can be reasonable for a limited task when the owner has time to learn and can verify the result.</p>
<p>It can produce a prototype, test service presentation, create a small information page or demonstrate a workflow.</p>
<p>RESET also works with people who started independently and need help finishing. Their work helps explain the concept and requirements.</p>
<p>We assess what works, where data lives, what can be extended and what needs changing.</p>
<p>Handover to specialists is possible, but completion costs require inspection. Finished screens may hide substantial integration, storage and error-handling work.</p>
<p>Even experienced developers need verification. In the 2025 Stack Overflow survey, 66% of respondents to the question on AI frustrations selected solutions that were almost right but needed fixing. This describes respondents' experience, not the error rate of all generated code. <a href="https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2025/ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stack Overflow Developer Survey 2025</a>.</p>
<h2 id="crm">Why custom CRM needs a separate estimate</h2>
<p>Websites typically start with visitor needs. A CRM reflects internal processes and their relationships.</p>
<p>One client may consider several properties, speak with multiple agents and return months later. History, ownership and deduplication need decisions.</p>
<p>Access rights, reports, existing data imports and service connections add requirements.</p>
<p>Before estimating custom development, identify what ready-made software covers and where specific logic is necessary. This establishes a justified scope.</p>
<p>AI may speed up functions, but company rules still need to be described and checked with their users.</p>
<h2 id="after-launch">Costs after launch</h2>
<p>Creation and operation should be discussed separately.</p>
<p>Domain, hosting, licences, integration maintenance, content updates and support may remain. Embedded AI can add model usage charges.</p>
<p>Some costs are fixed; others depend on load, users or processing.</p>
<p>Decide what the owner can edit. Requiring a developer for each price or photo update affects ownership costs.</p>
<p>Request recurring charges and future development terms before commissioning.</p>
<h2 id="save-budget">How to reduce the development budget</h2>
<p>The most practical saving is a clearly agreed first-version scope.</p>
<p>If an agency needs advertising for one development, start with that journey. Add a large catalogue, accounts and complex automation when demand is established.</p>
<p>Prepared materials, service access, process descriptions and an available decision-maker also help.</p>
<p>Prototypes resolve uncertainty early. Detailed requirements reduce different interpretations. AI accelerates suitable tasks within a clear plan.</p>
<p>Forms, data transfer and key actions still need adequate launch checks because the business relies on them.</p>
<h2 id="brief">What RESET needs for an estimate</h2>
<p>Describe what you want to create, who needs it and which problem it should solve.</p>
<ul class="ed-checklist"><li><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg><span>Business objective and intended users.</span></li><li><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg><span>Advertising and search plans.</span></li><li><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg><span>Data, services and integrations.</span></li><li><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg><span>Readiness of copy, images and translations.</span></li><li><svg class="ed-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="m5 12 4 4L19 6"/></svg><span>Target timing and first-version priorities.</span></li></ul><p>Existing sites, prototypes, references and self-built versions help define essentials, phases and scope.</p>
<p>RESET examples are NIVELLUX at $600, SHEPIT HOUSE at $1000 and Estate CRM for DELMAR at $2000. Each refers to an agreed scope; a new project is estimated by structure, content, functions and integrations.</p>
<p>AI creates opportunities to save effort. Clear documentation and systematic checking turn those savings into a product that meets agreed needs and supports future work.</p>
<h2 id="questions">Before starting</h2><details><summary>What does an AI-assisted website cost at RESET?</summary><p>Examples: NIVELLUX $600, SHEPIT HOUSE $1000 and Estate CRM for DELMAR $2000. These are specific scopes. New projects depend on structure, content, functionality and integrations.</p></details><details><summary>Is SEO included?</summary><p>SEO preparation is specified in the scope. Ongoing promotion, articles and new landing pages are agreed separately.</p></details><details><summary>Can you finish a site I built myself?</summary><p>Yes. We first inspect its condition and determine the remaining work.</p></details><details><summary>Will I pay for AI after launch?</summary><p>Using AI only during development does not itself create a subscription for the owner. Platforms and services may charge their own fees. Embedded AI features may need recurring payments.</p></details><h2 id="sources">Sources and editorial basis</h2><p>Prices and workflow are provided by RESET. Research findings include their task and observation period.</p><ol><li><a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2302.06590" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">The Impact of AI on Developer Productivity: Evidence from GitHub Copilot</a>. Controlled experiment, 2023.</li><li><a href="https://survey.stackoverflow.co/2025/ai" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Stack Overflow Developer Survey 2025</a>. AI experience section.</li></ol>
